    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74992" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθό-πους</span></b> , ὁ, ἡ, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πουν</span>, τό, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>upright on their feet,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. βαίνοντες ἄνις . . τιθήνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					419
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>steep,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρθόποδος ὑπὲρ πάγου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					985
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄρθιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρθόπαγον.</span></div>
